"ccaaff","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-03-06T19:01:03Z","updated_at":"2025-03-08T09:57:13Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.3\n\n### System information\n\nN/A\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe notification constants evaluate to numbers, and different constants can share the same number. For example, `CanvasItem.NOTIFICATION_DRAW` and `Window.NOTIFICATION_VISIBILITY_CHANGED` are both 30. This is [apparently](https://www.reddit.com/r/godot/comments/1ikrij3/notifications_reference_in_43/) not considered a problem because they're on different classes, and thus a single scene won't be getting both.\n\nBut this is still terrible design: if someone screws something up in some way, sending notifications to the wrong type of node, this will lead to confusing and hard-to-discover bugs in their application. It means that if someone is debugging and logs what notifications they're getting somewhere, they can't tell just from seeing the number what notification it is, and if they don't realize that duplicates exist, they might find that this number equals some other notification in the documentation and become confused why it's not acting that way.\n\nAs far as I can tell there's no good reason for this; it's not like we're going to run out of numbers.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nN/A\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\